                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "f42facbf-2fc9-4db7-a6e3-eeca71f3eb2c",
                        "entry_id": "bcee4c19-3098-3023-bcb6-5e5a26362de9",
                        "tags": [
                            "adverbial",
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "генери́ровавши"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "12061e13-e379-4806-94f0-3e5700e6022c",
                        "entry_id": "bcee4c19-3098-3023-bcb6-5e5a26362de9",
                        "tags": [
                            "future"
                        ],
                        "form": "буду/будешь… генери́ровать"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3f1a8602-fbc2-3019-91a0-5d9711bf832b",
                        "entry_id": "bcee4c19-3098-3023-bcb6-5e5a26362de9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. порождать, производить, создавать"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c65724d1-7a26-4498-aefe-ca613486a069",
                                "sense_id": "3f1a8602-fbc2-3019-91a0-5d9711bf832b",
                                "text": "Если при сборке передатчика не было допущено ошибок, то он начинает генерировать колебания."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e1d15920-d8e5-49cb-98f7-c4720b37adfb",
                                "sense_id": "3f1a8602-fbc2-3019-91a0-5d9711bf832b",
                                "text": "Одна из основных особенностей нейрона — это способность клетки генерировать различные электрические потенциалы."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0df4f9e8-91e4-4f58-ae92-18c29a06d36b",
                                "sense_id": "3f1a8602-fbc2-3019-91a0-5d9711bf832b",
                                "text": "Мокер оправдывался: — Я генерирую идеи… Баскина раздражало слово «генерирую»."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e1edca52-9219-4aa1-bc57-14d4223060d1",
                                "sense_id": "3f1a8602-fbc2-3019-91a0-5d9711bf832b",
                                "text": "Алгоритм шифрует данные по 56-разрядному ключу и может генерировать до 72×10¹⁵ уникальных ключей."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "de118821-e28e-4b63-901a-70205b23153c",
                        "source_entry_id": "bcee4c19-3098-3023-bcb6-5e5a26362de9",
                        "source_sense_id": "3f1a8602-fbc2-3019-91a0-5d9711bf832b",
                        "target_lang_word": "generate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "generate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ce56fa79-e923-35a6-a04e-222cd98891cf",
                                        "entry_id": "6125309d-0667-3e6a-a588-9f3a31d98d4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To bring into being; give rise to."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aaffa184-4a79-4f97-be3e-d02915da7b7b",
                                                "sense_id": "ce56fa79-e923-35a6-a04e-222cd98891cf",
                                                "text": "The discussion generated an uproar."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70cdb9f9-c3a8-4d18-a811-ad249ec75d0a",
                                                "sense_id": "ce56fa79-e923-35a6-a04e-222cd98891cf",
                                                "text": "The Ecclesiastical Commission was generated by Sir Robert Peel and bore the marks of Peel’s personality; bureaucratic, capable and cold."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ffaeb7c9-6c65-4205-8f08-385ec2b7bede",
                                                "sense_id": "ce56fa79-e923-35a6-a04e-222cd98891cf",
                                                "text": "In the last 20 minutes Athletic began to generate the sort of pressure of which they are capable, but by then it was far too late: the game had begun to slip away from them as early as the seventh minute."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98c9f6f8-a2a0-41fc-8020-1f7c775deebd",
                                                "sense_id": "ce56fa79-e923-35a6-a04e-222cd98891cf",
                                                "text": "The ability to shift profits to low-tax countries by locating intellectual property in them[…]is often assumed to be the preserve of high-tech companies.[…]current tax rules make it easy for all sorts of firms to generate[…]“stateless income”: profit subject to tax in a jurisdiction that is neither the location of the factors of production that generate the income nor where the parent firm is domiciled."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d51c0612-a402-32b1-89b8-ae66ceefc3b5",
                                        "entry_id": "6125309d-0667-3e6a-a588-9f3a31d98d4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To produce as a result of a chemical or physical process."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f1d0eec-630e-45de-bb34-f63cf5ee58f8",
                                                "sense_id": "d51c0612-a402-32b1-89b8-ae66ceefc3b5",
                                                "text": "Adding concentrated sulphuric acid to water generates heat."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e10a5aab-9a1e-37d6-b180-7aa3d2ac4cd5",
                                        "entry_id": "6125309d-0667-3e6a-a588-9f3a31d98d4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To procreate, beget."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfe03e16-873c-4c92-bd2f-8a643072401b",
                                                "sense_id": "e10a5aab-9a1e-37d6-b180-7aa3d2ac4cd5",
                                                "text": "They generated many offspring."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "24c56485-0b09-3e9a-8df0-f5d5432f363a",
                                        "entry_id": "6125309d-0667-3e6a-a588-9f3a31d98d4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To form a figure from a curve or solid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3282921-9e07-4c10-a379-b7e09dc65d54",
                                                "sense_id": "24c56485-0b09-3e9a-8df0-f5d5432f363a",
                                                "text": "Rotating a circle generates a sphere."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "84e2f891-7382-3b89-917e-874a773a56ab",
                                        "entry_id": "6125309d-0667-3e6a-a588-9f3a31d98d4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To appear or occur; be generated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8084ec9-6d36-4840-a50c-8be5bbb71c32",
                                                "sense_id": "84e2f891-7382-3b89-917e-874a773a56ab",
                                                "text": "Mrs. Fennel, seeing the steam begin to generate on the countenances of her guests, crossed over and touched the fiddler's elbow and put her hand on the serpent's mouth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "generate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "110c2f74-b48f-3308-bbce-c4e56007464d",
                                        "entry_id": "203dbf64-cf40-3186-a641-8883f7b69ffa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Generated, not self-existent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f68d8b32-1d8f-493f-b5a3-bc0eee8123f3",
                                                "sense_id": "110c2f74-b48f-3308-bbce-c4e56007464d",
                                                "text": "But neither is one time generated in another; for if the preſent be generated in the future, the future muſt be present; and if in the paſt, the paſt. The ſame may be ſaid of other times; therefore one time is not generated in another. Now if time be neither generated in itſelf, nor one time in another, it is not generate at all. But that it is not ingenerate, we ſhewed also. Therefore ſeeing it is neither generate nor ingenerate, it is not at all; for every Beeing muſt either be generate or ingenerate."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4850d6f6-0259-4410-aad0-734f39c2e6f5",
                                                "sense_id": "110c2f74-b48f-3308-bbce-c4e56007464d",
                                                "text": "It poses the thorny problem of the status of the Logos. Is he generate or ingenerate?.. Justin replies that he is generate—but in a special sense."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
